  "name": "scaled_weight_boundary",
  "description": "Integer half-up weight scaling: (w + s//2) // s. Pins the .5 boundary, where Python's round() (half-to-even) and JavaScript's Math.round() (half-up) disagree. A float implementation passes every other case here and fails only these, producing different aggregates from identical ballots.",
